1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:01,310
[Viewer discretion is advised due to violence, self-harm, and potentially triggering scenes.]
[Exclusive: Faceless singer Yul suspected of involvement in classmate's disappearance]

2
00:00:01,550 --> 00:00:02,080
[No wonder he doesn't show his face.]

3
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:02,580
[This student used to work part-time at our store.
No wonder he never gave me his ID.]

4
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:03,090
[Could the disappearance mean he killed someone and buried them?]
[He definitely killed someone.]

5
00:00:03,210 --> 00:00:04,490
[Reported] [Could he be the murderer?] [Definitely a murderer.] [Gonna leave the industry.] [Yul eliminated.] [Show your face.]
[His classmates should come out and say something.] [I was a fan. How disappointing.]

6
00:00:05,660 --> 00:00:06,950
[[Breaking News] Expected release
of interviews with classmates at the time]

7
00:00:07,270 --> 00:00:08,580
[[Update] Obtained testimonies from school personnel at the time of the incident]
[[Breaking News] Expected release of interviews with classmates at the time]

8
00:00:08,760 --> 00:00:10,170
[Yul missing case] [Faceless singer Yul suspected of involvement in classmate's disappearance]
[Popular faceless singer Yul allegedly involved in classmate's missing persons case]

9
00:00:10,180 --> 00:00:34,450
[Interviews with classmates regarding
rookie singer Yul's past school violence controversy]

10
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:13,180
That Yul is Lee Hanyul.

11
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:14,820
He was our schoolmate.

12
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:18,570
As far as I know,
Lee Hanyul and Adolph were really close.

13
00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:20,310
I even have a video,

14
00:00:20,430 --> 00:00:21,760
taken in the school gym.

15
00:00:21,850 --> 00:00:24,010
The way Lee Hanyul treated him...

16
00:00:24,250 --> 00:00:27,730
Anyway, Adolph disappeared after that.

17
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:29,870
I heard he might be dead.

18
00:00:30,740 --> 00:00:32,000
Lee Hanyul killed him.

19
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,370
Killed his own friend. What a psycho.

20
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:36,940
Suppress the video.

21
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:40,040
Find those two bastards in the video
claiming to be Hanyul's classmates first.

22
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:42,770
Once you find them,
bring them to me immediately.

23
00:00:52,370 --> 00:00:53,400
Hey, Pan.

24
00:00:54,010 --> 00:00:55,710
You're with Hanyul now, right?

25
00:00:55,710 --> 00:00:57,310
I'm going to find Hanyul now.

26
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:21,170
Our Lee Won has grown wings,

27
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:23,450
even stabbing me in the back.

28
00:01:24,490 --> 00:01:25,820
It's amazing, isn't it?

29
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:29,270
It doesn't even take a day
to ruin someone.

30
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:34,280
Ah, and the one being ruined is me—

31
00:01:36,770 --> 00:01:39,240
Not that damn little brat.

32
00:01:45,020 --> 00:01:47,550
Now everyone knows that kid

33
00:01:47,670 --> 00:01:50,750
was brought up single-handedly by
our company's CEO, composer Lee Won.

34
00:01:50,750 --> 00:01:51,990
I'm the one bearing all the losses,

35
00:01:51,990 --> 00:01:53,039
don't you think?

36
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:04,920
Back then, his parents...

37
00:02:05,050 --> 00:02:07,820
How much did they sell that kid for?

38
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:09,550
Do you remember?

39
00:02:10,530 --> 00:02:11,750
Let me think.

40
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:14,880
It was about 10 million won back then.

41
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,950
Considering inflation, it should be about

42
00:02:18,070 --> 00:02:19,590
a billion now?

43
00:02:22,490 --> 00:02:23,940
Thanks, Won.

44
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:28,140
Thank you for helping me find the rascal
who owed me a billion

45
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:30,150
and ran away from me.

46
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:33,020
He's in good health, right?

47
00:02:33,370 --> 00:02:35,320
Doesn't smoke or drink, right?

48
00:02:35,470 --> 00:02:38,840
After all, every organ of his
is a precious commodity.

49
00:02:39,650 --> 00:02:40,880
All right.

50
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:44,070
Now it's time to keep your promise, Won.

51
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:47,530
That thing you promised me.

52
00:02:50,550 --> 00:02:51,740
[Collateral Contract
Name: Kim Jaeseok]

53
00:02:52,670 --> 00:02:54,040
Ten million won.

54
00:02:55,540 --> 00:02:58,390
Just a kid, what use can he be?

55
00:02:59,460 --> 00:03:02,000
We'll use him as bait for the next plan.

56
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:03,300
Lock him up first.

57
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:06,610
I'm scared.

58
00:03:07,530 --> 00:03:08,930
Where's Mom?

59
00:03:12,410 --> 00:03:13,500
Boss,

60
00:03:14,150 --> 00:03:16,320
this kid doesn't belong here.

61
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:22,590
Won,

62
00:03:23,890 --> 00:03:24,930
do you know him?

63
00:03:25,150 --> 00:03:26,110
No,

64
00:03:26,370 --> 00:03:27,400
I don't know him.

65
00:03:27,910 --> 00:03:29,180
Then why?

66
00:03:29,780 --> 00:03:31,370
Please give me some time,

67
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:35,950
until this kid grows up
enough to be useful.

68
00:03:43,050 --> 00:03:46,010
Then what do I get in the meantime?

69
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:48,810
I'll do anything.

70
00:03:49,380 --> 00:03:52,090
I'll do his share too.

71
00:03:52,390 --> 00:03:53,480
Please.

72
00:03:55,810 --> 00:03:56,890
All right then.

73
00:03:57,340 --> 00:03:59,480
This is the first time our Won
has begged me.

74
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:01,160
I have to grant your request.

75
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,520
Then starting today,

76
00:04:04,660 --> 00:04:08,240
you'll be responsible
for that kid's share.

77
00:04:18,820 --> 00:04:20,279
I did as you said.

78
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:22,890
I waited for him to grow up,

79
00:04:23,110 --> 00:04:24,790
but that kid suddenly ran away.

80
00:04:24,790 --> 00:04:25,830
Right?

81
00:04:26,990 --> 00:04:28,050
Bring him here—

82
00:04:28,210 --> 00:04:30,500
right now, immediately.

83
00:04:32,780 --> 00:04:34,490
Just give me a week.

84
00:04:41,150 --> 00:04:43,560
Whether it was back then or now—

85
00:04:45,260 --> 00:04:48,870
what does that kid mean to you, Won?

86
00:04:50,650 --> 00:04:52,750
I'm begging you for the last time.

87
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:02,250
If he disappears like he did back then,

88
00:05:03,270 --> 00:05:05,500
you'll have to pay me 3 times as much—no—

89
00:05:08,660 --> 00:05:11,120
you'll have to pay me
dozens of times as much.

90
00:05:21,860 --> 00:05:24,140
Your parents sold you to me

91
00:05:24,310 --> 00:05:26,050
for a mere 5 million won.

92
00:05:36,140 --> 00:05:39,140
You should be of great use.

93
00:05:48,830 --> 00:05:55,420
[Some scenes were created with AI.]

94
00:05:57,659 --> 00:06:01,400
[Adapted from the webtoon
"The Sound of Sugar Cubes" by Kim Tak]

95
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:04,200
[Screenwriter: So-on (JD)]

96
00:06:04,210 --> 00:06:07,180
[Director: Yoon Jinyoung]

97
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:25,250
[Yoo Dohyun]

98
00:06:25,250 --> 00:06:26,840
[Cho Chanhyeon]

99
00:06:26,850 --> 00:06:28,540
[Ko Gyeol]

100
00:06:29,990 --> 00:06:33,440
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

101
00:06:47,530 --> 00:06:48,930
These darn reporters...

102
00:06:49,340 --> 00:06:50,320
Damn it.

103
00:06:51,710 --> 00:06:52,690
Forget it.

104
00:07:04,290 --> 00:07:09,870
Why is the hourly wage
for handing out flyers so low lately?

105
00:07:10,220 --> 00:07:12,030
How is anyone supposed to make a living?

106
00:07:12,030 --> 00:07:12,570
Right?

107
00:07:12,730 --> 00:07:15,150
Life is too hard.

108
00:07:16,710 --> 00:07:18,630
It's too hard, paying so little.

109
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,430
Excuse me.

110
00:07:21,260 --> 00:07:22,390
Damn it.

111
00:07:35,180 --> 00:07:36,380
Hey, hey.

112
00:07:36,820 --> 00:07:38,710
You want to go out?

113
00:07:38,830 --> 00:07:40,460
They came for me.

114
00:07:41,720 --> 00:07:43,800
I don't want to cause you trouble.

115
00:07:44,050 --> 00:07:46,810
So what? Will going out now
solve the problem?

116
00:07:49,230 --> 00:07:51,030
Lee Won will be here soon.

117
00:07:51,360 --> 00:07:53,350
Regardless of if he's here
to save the day or ruin it—

118
00:07:53,350 --> 00:07:55,320
anyway, he'll definitely come.

119
00:07:55,470 --> 00:07:56,850
Just sit down and wait for him, you brat.

120
00:07:56,850 --> 00:07:57,850
Seriously.

121
00:07:58,420 --> 00:07:59,940
You scared me.

122
00:08:01,580 --> 00:08:02,460
How did you get in?

123
00:08:02,460 --> 00:08:04,660
There are a bunch of reporters outside.

124
00:08:04,900 --> 00:08:06,630
I came in through the back door.

125
00:08:07,130 --> 00:08:09,060
How do you know about the back door?

126
00:08:09,150 --> 00:08:10,800
I've been here so many times.

127
00:08:11,350 --> 00:08:12,500
I see.

128
00:08:12,850 --> 00:08:15,250
But now this back door is as good as gone.

129
00:08:15,550 --> 00:08:16,450
Why?

130
00:08:16,910 --> 00:08:18,360
Those reporters saw me.

131
00:08:19,860 --> 00:08:23,260
You brat, you're here to ruin things.

132
00:08:23,470 --> 00:08:26,130
You've completely
turned us into rats in a trap.

133
00:08:26,280 --> 00:08:27,320
Damn it.

134
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:39,909
Why did you risk coming here?

135
00:08:41,750 --> 00:08:44,350
Getting involved with me
won't do you any good.

136
00:08:46,140 --> 00:08:48,470
I love getting involved with you the most.

137
00:08:49,110 --> 00:08:50,440
It excites me.

138
00:08:51,730 --> 00:08:53,160
Excites you?

139
00:08:54,370 --> 00:08:57,860
Well, given how thrilling
the situation is now, I guess.

140
00:09:03,890 --> 00:09:05,010
Hanyul.

141
00:09:09,240 --> 00:09:10,770
Run away with me.

142
00:09:12,980 --> 00:09:14,050
What?

143
00:09:15,270 --> 00:09:17,000
I said let's run away together—

144
00:09:17,680 --> 00:09:19,140
to somewhere far away.

145
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:22,650
To a place where no one can find us.

146
00:09:24,610 --> 00:09:25,840
I don't want to.

147
00:09:27,210 --> 00:09:29,120
I don't want to run anymore.

148
00:09:30,330 --> 00:09:34,930
I will never hide like a coward again.

149
00:09:38,780 --> 00:09:39,820
Good.

150
00:09:41,520 --> 00:09:43,520
That's the Lee Hanyul I know.

151
00:09:50,090 --> 00:09:52,430
Is something wrong with you?

152
00:10:00,410 --> 00:10:01,450
Pan.

153
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:05,580
I have a favor to ask.

154
00:10:06,980 --> 00:10:08,580
Wh-What is it?

155
00:10:13,310 --> 00:10:14,940
It's Lee Hanyul.

156
00:10:16,140 --> 00:10:17,930
No, Lee Hanyul is over there.

157
00:10:18,050 --> 00:10:19,100
Lee Hanyul! Lee Hanyul!

158
00:10:19,100 --> 00:10:20,640
-Where? Where?
-Here! Here! Lee Hanyul!

159
00:10:20,640 --> 00:10:21,870
-Lee Hanyul!
-Hurry, hurry, hurry!

160
00:10:21,870 --> 00:10:22,900
Lee Hanyul!

161
00:10:23,310 --> 00:10:24,390
Catch him!

162
00:10:39,250 --> 00:10:40,760
Where are we going?

163
00:10:42,170 --> 00:10:43,830
I'm asking where we are going.

164
00:10:46,340 --> 00:10:47,620
To find Adolph.

165
00:10:48,710 --> 00:10:49,980
Adolph?

166
00:10:50,660 --> 00:10:51,650
Yeah.

167
00:11:36,310 --> 00:11:37,680
He's sleeping.

168
00:11:38,880 --> 00:11:40,880
He was in a coma before.

169
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:43,060
He just woke up not long ago.

170
00:11:44,730 --> 00:11:46,200
Why...

171
00:11:46,830 --> 00:11:48,390
Why is he here...

172
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:52,180
I'll tell you everything slowly.

173
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:54,890
Calm down first.

174
00:12:01,710 --> 00:12:03,760
[Herod, I'm on the roof of your hospital.
If you don't come in 5 minutes, I'll jump.]

175
00:12:13,790 --> 00:12:14,870
Herod.

176
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:20,040
What are you doing right now?

177
00:12:26,780 --> 00:12:28,750
What are you trying to do, you bastard?

178
00:12:28,750 --> 00:12:30,880
You should be thanking me, Hanyul.

179
00:12:31,190 --> 00:12:32,640
What? You bastard!

180
00:12:33,260 --> 00:12:36,120
I was really the one
taking care of Adolph all along.

181
00:12:37,010 --> 00:12:40,030
It was that guy Lee Won
who suddenly took him away.

182
00:12:41,560 --> 00:12:43,810
Then why didn't you tell me before?

183
00:12:44,460 --> 00:12:47,050
Even if you were scared,
you shouldn't have kept it a secret.

184
00:12:47,050 --> 00:12:48,290
If you knew,

185
00:12:50,580 --> 00:12:52,100
you would have gone to him.

186
00:12:53,670 --> 00:12:55,680
If you went to him,

187
00:12:57,220 --> 00:12:59,370
I would become useless again.

188
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:01,900
Is that why you made Adolph like that?

189
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:04,950
He was your friend!

190
00:13:05,390 --> 00:13:08,850
How many times do I have to say
it wasn't me for you to believe it?

191
00:13:09,870 --> 00:13:11,580
Still denying...

192
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:13,510
I saw you.

193
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:17,740
I saw you were there, you bastard!

194
00:13:21,510 --> 00:13:23,330
Go to hell, you bastard!

195
00:13:23,910 --> 00:13:24,860
This is amazing.

196
00:13:25,090 --> 00:13:26,650
Are you filming?

197
00:13:29,420 --> 00:13:31,630
The reason I went there...

198
00:13:31,880 --> 00:13:33,600
I mean, I was there for...

199
00:13:33,730 --> 00:13:35,480
You wanted Adolph dead.

200
00:13:36,190 --> 00:13:37,390
Didn't you?

201
00:13:37,630 --> 00:13:38,930
Say it.

202
00:13:39,690 --> 00:13:41,630
Herod likes Lee Hanyul.

203
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:44,680
But Lee Hanyul sticks
with this guy all day long.

204
00:13:44,750 --> 00:13:46,210
This guy is quite likable.

205
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,250
Oh, you're here.

206
00:13:48,910 --> 00:13:51,170
Look at his face. It's hilarious, right?

207
00:13:51,710 --> 00:13:56,420
Dare you say you never had
such a thought even for a moment?

208
00:14:01,750 --> 00:14:02,950
Hey, hey.

209
00:14:03,650 --> 00:14:05,060
Shall we take a photo?

210
00:14:05,780 --> 00:14:06,840
Look here.

211
00:14:10,460 --> 00:14:11,650
I...

212
00:14:13,030 --> 00:14:15,430
I only wanted you to be by my side.

213
00:14:16,140 --> 00:14:17,370
I...

214
00:14:18,570 --> 00:14:20,540
I've always been by your side.

215
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:23,380
You didn't have to get rid of anyone.

216
00:14:24,790 --> 00:14:27,100
I would have walked to your side myself.

217
00:14:28,540 --> 00:14:29,900
You're lying.

218
00:14:31,330 --> 00:14:33,180
When you needed me,

219
00:14:33,670 --> 00:14:35,740
was I ever not by your side?

220
00:14:36,870 --> 00:14:38,580
I liked you.

221
00:14:40,260 --> 00:14:41,890
Very much.

222
00:14:45,990 --> 00:14:47,200
Hanyul.

223
00:14:48,730 --> 00:14:50,280
I'm sorry.

224
00:14:51,130 --> 00:14:52,330
I liked you too much.

225
00:14:52,510 --> 00:14:53,440
No.

226
00:14:56,740 --> 00:14:58,370
You didn't like me.

227
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:02,550
You loved the way you looked
when you liked me.

228
00:15:04,950 --> 00:15:06,050
Hanyul.

229
00:15:06,750 --> 00:15:08,440
Let's start over.

230
00:15:08,960 --> 00:15:11,390
Adolph, you, and me. Let's start over...

231
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:13,700
No.

232
00:15:14,890 --> 00:15:16,250
Over my dead body.

233
00:15:18,390 --> 00:15:21,120
Don't ever appear
in front of Adolph and me again.

234
00:15:25,400 --> 00:15:26,580
Hanyul.

235
00:15:28,770 --> 00:15:30,210
Just once...

236
00:15:30,570 --> 00:15:32,760
Can you hug me just once?

237
00:15:33,890 --> 00:15:35,570
I'm sorry.

238
00:15:37,560 --> 00:15:38,880
Hanyul.

239
00:15:40,490 --> 00:15:44,510
If you want to apologize, go to Adolph.

240
00:15:44,830 --> 00:15:46,340
Don't apologize to me.

241
00:15:59,780 --> 00:16:01,070
It's my fault.

242
00:16:07,880 --> 00:16:09,380
It's all my fault.

243
00:16:36,670 --> 00:16:37,710
Where did you go?

244
00:16:37,880 --> 00:16:39,540
You didn't answer your phone.

245
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:41,930
I just went out for a bit.

246
00:16:42,690 --> 00:16:43,910
Did...

247
00:16:46,010 --> 00:16:47,210
Did you cry?

248
00:16:47,630 --> 00:16:49,250
I didn't cry.

249
00:16:51,280 --> 00:16:53,420
Do you know how long
we've been looking for you?

250
00:16:53,420 --> 00:16:55,160
I was only gone for 10 minutes.

251
00:16:55,520 --> 00:16:57,600
Not me. It was...

252
00:17:01,490 --> 00:17:02,700
Lee Hanyul!

253
00:17:11,089 --> 00:17:12,250
Adolph!

254
00:17:18,920 --> 00:17:20,960
[Strict bed rest]

255
00:17:28,550 --> 00:17:31,130
Hanyul, don't you think I'm really lucky?

256
00:17:31,270 --> 00:17:32,460
I heard that if it were anyone else,

257
00:17:32,460 --> 00:17:35,460
they would have died on the spot
in such a huge traffic accident.

258
00:17:35,460 --> 00:17:38,120
I feel like I just woke up
from a long sleep.

259
00:17:38,730 --> 00:17:41,250
But they said I can't walk yet.

260
00:17:41,380 --> 00:17:43,950
Something about lying down
for too long or whatever.

261
00:17:43,950 --> 00:17:46,660
He still doesn't know
what he went through.

262
00:17:46,810 --> 00:17:48,580
So I just made up some excuses.

263
00:17:49,320 --> 00:17:52,690
Why would you say it was a huge traffic accident
where he could've died on the spot.

264
00:17:52,690 --> 00:17:55,910
Also, do you know how surprised I was
when I opened my eyes?

265
00:17:56,070 --> 00:17:59,940
The famous composer Lee Won
was right in front of me...

266
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:02,540
Hanyul, you remember, right?

267
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:04,630
I said I wanted to be a composer
like Lee Won.

268
00:18:04,630 --> 00:18:06,310
Of course, I remember.

269
00:18:08,580 --> 00:18:12,220
I wrote a song called "Sound of Dawn."

270
00:18:12,360 --> 00:18:14,700
Could you listen to it,

271
00:18:14,970 --> 00:18:15,910
please?

272
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:18,020
Ah, sure.

273
00:18:18,310 --> 00:18:19,600
I'm all ears.

274
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:24,720
By the way, where is Herod?

275
00:18:26,290 --> 00:18:27,400
Ah...

276
00:18:27,730 --> 00:18:28,670
Herod.

277
00:18:28,780 --> 00:18:29,940
Herod.

278
00:18:30,180 --> 00:18:33,980
Seriously, this guy Herod.
His good friend woke up after a few years.

279
00:18:34,730 --> 00:18:36,000
Where did he go?

280
00:18:36,760 --> 00:18:38,190
Herod... Well...

281
00:18:38,370 --> 00:18:39,410
He's dead.

282
00:18:40,280 --> 00:18:41,390
Huh?

283
00:18:42,300 --> 00:18:43,160
That's not it.

284
00:18:43,340 --> 00:18:44,290
I mean, Herod...

285
00:18:44,410 --> 00:18:46,450
I should have killed him,
but I couldn't do it.

286
00:18:46,450 --> 00:18:47,660
He'll be dead soon.

287
00:18:49,860 --> 00:18:52,670
Herod was super worried about you.

288
00:18:52,790 --> 00:18:56,650
He probably didn't come because
he wasn't told that you're awake yet.

289
00:18:57,180 --> 00:18:59,460
Although I don't remember clearly,

290
00:18:59,640 --> 00:19:01,300
in my last memories, Herod...

291
00:19:01,560 --> 00:19:02,730
That's it.

292
00:19:05,230 --> 00:19:07,150
Let's stop here for today.

293
00:19:07,890 --> 00:19:10,570
Slowly recall the rest later on.

294
00:19:10,940 --> 00:19:12,810
Mm, got it.

295
00:19:14,670 --> 00:19:16,180
But thank god!

296
00:19:18,430 --> 00:19:20,060
He's on strict bed rest.

297
00:19:24,010 --> 00:19:25,490
-Have you been well?
-Yeah.

298
00:19:25,320 --> 00:19:26,730
[Secretary]

299
00:19:26,650 --> 00:19:27,570
Are you singing?

300
00:19:27,570 --> 00:19:28,460
I'm still singing.

301
00:19:28,460 --> 00:19:29,240
What about composing?

302
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:30,370
I'm also composing.

303
00:19:30,450 --> 00:19:31,980
-You're composing?
-Yeah.

304
00:19:31,980 --> 00:19:33,310
What are you composing?

305
00:19:42,730 --> 00:19:43,970
No.

306
00:19:45,160 --> 00:19:46,700
Over my dead body.

307
00:19:47,870 --> 00:19:50,600
Don't ever appear
in front of Adolph and me again.

308
00:20:01,340 --> 00:20:02,570
Hello, it's me.

309
00:20:05,160 --> 00:20:09,220
Do you still have the phone numbers
of those classmates from high school?

310
00:20:14,220 --> 00:20:15,340
Oh, okay.

311
00:20:16,570 --> 00:20:18,730
You said you found
those bastard classmates?

312
00:20:18,730 --> 00:20:19,710
Yes.

313
00:20:20,620 --> 00:20:23,220
Right at the entrance
of our company building.

314
00:20:23,950 --> 00:20:26,190
I clearly hit harder, idiot.

315
00:20:26,320 --> 00:20:29,650
Looks like they are here
to extort some money with the video.

316
00:20:31,170 --> 00:20:32,200
Yes.

317
00:20:35,600 --> 00:20:36,640
Then let's play
rock-paper-scissors. Damn it.

318
00:20:36,640 --> 00:20:37,360
Why play rock-paper-scissors?

319
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:38,380
-No.
-Just play rock-paper-scissors.

320
00:20:38,380 --> 00:20:39,710
Rock-paper-scissors.

321
00:20:39,760 --> 00:20:40,700
Damn it.

322
00:20:41,560 --> 00:20:42,830
You scared me.

323
00:20:43,890 --> 00:20:45,020
Who are you?

324
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:02,730
So what?

325
00:21:03,420 --> 00:21:05,810
Lee Hanyul isn't in this video.

326
00:21:06,360 --> 00:21:08,580
Well...

327
00:21:08,730 --> 00:21:10,490
H-Herod is in it.

328
00:21:10,680 --> 00:21:11,590
Yeah.

329
00:21:12,440 --> 00:21:13,230
Herod?

330
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:14,170
Yes.

331
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:16,300
Herod is also a singer
under your company, right?

332
00:21:16,300 --> 00:21:18,860
Compared to Lee Hanyul,
Herod is more popular, right?

333
00:21:18,860 --> 00:21:21,720
It will probably bring
a bigger blow to the company.

334
00:21:28,190 --> 00:21:30,360
So no matter what,

335
00:21:30,870 --> 00:21:33,710
your claims that
the video captured Lee Hanyul

336
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:37,050
and that he killed his friend

337
00:21:37,520 --> 00:21:40,020
are all lies you made up.

338
00:21:41,740 --> 00:21:43,470
If you don't want it, forget it.

339
00:21:43,490 --> 00:21:44,710
Hey, let's go.

340
00:21:44,990 --> 00:21:46,510
Herod called just now, right?

341
00:21:46,510 --> 00:21:47,460
Yeah.

342
00:21:47,620 --> 00:21:49,740
Let's go sell it to him. Let's go.

343
00:21:54,260 --> 00:21:55,330
What are you doing?

344
00:21:55,460 --> 00:21:57,320
Didn't you say you don't need this video?

345
00:21:57,320 --> 00:21:58,560
I mean.

346
00:21:58,770 --> 00:22:01,170
The fact that Lee Hanyul
isn't in this video

347
00:22:01,280 --> 00:22:04,480
is enough to prove
he has nothing to do with this incident.

348
00:22:07,850 --> 00:22:09,180
Time to take a beating.

349
00:22:10,150 --> 00:22:11,310
I promise you.

350
00:22:13,960 --> 00:22:15,860
As long as you stay by my side,

351
00:22:16,010 --> 00:22:18,200
I won't let anyone get hurt.

352
00:22:31,520 --> 00:22:34,820
You should be glad
I'm much easier to talk to lately.

353
00:22:35,340 --> 00:22:36,410
Go.

354
00:22:36,600 --> 00:22:38,580
Hurry up. Hurry up.

355
00:22:55,430 --> 00:22:57,060
These rascals—

356
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:18,790
With this, Hanyul can live.

357
00:23:20,870 --> 00:23:23,140
Without this, you can live, right?

358
00:23:31,690 --> 00:23:32,970
Take it.

359
00:23:41,350 --> 00:23:43,650
This is your only chance.

360
00:24:04,520 --> 00:24:08,080
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

361
00:24:07,980 --> 00:24:09,580
It's been a while, Herod.

362
00:24:09,720 --> 00:24:11,190
It's me, Shinyoung.

363
00:24:11,380 --> 00:24:13,200
Ah, you don't remember?

364
00:24:13,400 --> 00:24:14,400
That's quite sad.

365
00:24:14,570 --> 00:24:16,560
If I say this,
will you remember something?

366
00:24:16,560 --> 00:24:18,650
The one who was with Adolph at the end.

367
00:24:18,820 --> 00:24:20,570
I see you're quite popular lately.

368
00:24:20,570 --> 00:24:21,950
You must have made a lot of money, right?

369
00:24:21,950 --> 00:24:24,980
How dare you trick me, you bastard.

370
00:24:26,330 --> 00:24:28,700
Go die.

371
00:24:30,310 --> 00:24:31,340
Lee Won!

372
00:24:31,490 --> 00:24:32,540
[Hanyul]

373
00:24:33,090 --> 00:24:34,810
Fake contract for performance fees,

374
00:24:34,810 --> 00:24:36,320
paper company outsourcing contracts,

375
00:24:36,320 --> 00:24:37,550
operating a business
under a borrowed name,

376
00:24:37,550 --> 00:24:38,680
[Fake contract for performance fees, paper company outsourcing contracts, operating a business
under a borrowed name, designing a slush fund structure]

377
00:24:37,620 --> 00:24:39,710
designing a slush fund structure.

378
00:24:39,870 --> 00:24:43,410
The Lee Won I know
does whatever the boss tells him to do.
